Question

Calculate cumulative sales by date.

Expected output:

| order_date | amount | running_total |
| ---------- | ------ | ------------- |
| 2024-01-01 | 100    | 100           |
| 2024-01-02 | 200    | 300           |
| 2024-01-03 | 150    | 450           |
| 2024-01-04 | 250    | 700           | -->

#SQL

select 
order_date,amount,
sum(amount) over (order by order_date asc
rows between unbounded preceeding and current row) as running_total
from orders

#when we have multiple categories and we want to calculate the cumulative sales for each category separately, we can use the following SQL query:
select 
order_date,amount,
sum(amount) over (partition by category 
order by date asc
rows between unbounded preceeding and current row)
as running_total 
from orders

